From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:18:02 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Review round 1: collective-safe reductions, local
 tolerance, one connected chain

- The per-point reductions in the empty-or-partial check (distances under
  MIN, the inside mask under MAX) passed NumPy arrays to mpi4py's pickling
  allreduce, which compares whole arrays under MIN/MAX and raised on the
  combining rank while the others waited: every 2-D add_fault cut and
  every labelled add_conforming_surface hung at np >= 2 (Linux server
  review). They are now in-place Allreduce on buffers.
- The coverage tolerance is half the LOCAL median edge length at each
  trace point (the edges whose midpoints lie within 3x the nearest-midpoint
  distance, their lengths gathered over the ranks), not a count-weighted
  mean over the trace's box, which a graded mesh made 0.1 local cells in
  one place and 2-3 in another.
- add_fault now refuses a cut that is not ONE connected chain. Counted
  globally: the labelled edges are gathered and joined at end points
  keyed by coordinates (a shared vertex has identical coordinates on
  every rank), so a chain crossing a seam counts once. A chain in pieces
  could pass the distance test when the trace ran within half a cell of
  another piece; the split then split one piece, left the other labelled
  but unsplit, and add_fault returned the fault split along part of its
  length (on development, 101 of 265 sharp-kink faults it returned). A
  chain cut by an already-split fault's slit defers to the split's own
  touching-junction refusal.
- add_conforming_surface's refusal gives advice for a surface, not
  add_fault's resampling advice.
- The flat-cell guard's per-cell loop is vectorised (closure_points); its
  message no longer asks for a sample at a turn that is already one.
- The chord rule's comment no longer claims a 120-degree kink is always
  admitted (an off-centre one is refused sooner).

test_0897 gains a hand-labelled chain in two pieces with a one-edge gap,
which only the piece count refuses. The fault, conforming-surface and
line-cut suites: 431 passed, 1 skipped. Not run in parallel here (np 2-4
is the review's).

